      "passed": true,
      "status": "completed",
      "summary": "StaticFilesHandlerMixin defines only the synchronous get_response and no get_response_async. ASGIStaticFilesHandler.__call__ forwards matching requests to ASGIHandler.__call__, which awaits self.get_response_async inherited from BaseHandler; since the mixin's load_middleware is a no-op, self._middleware_chain is None and the await raises TypeError: 'NoneType' object is not callable. The fix is to add an async get_response_async to the mixin mirroring the sync get_response: serve via await sync_to_async(self.serve, thread_sensitive=True)(request) and return response_for_exception(request, e) on Http404 (the existing response_for_exception/Http404 imports already cover the sync branch). This requires importing asgiref.sync.sync_to_async in handlers.py. No existing tests exercise ASGIStaticFilesHandler, so a new tests/staticfiles_tests/test_handlers.py should cover a served static path, a fall-through path, and the DEBUG 404 branch.",
